From: eduke32-net transport branch
Subject: [PATCH] pages.yml: build + ship the multiplayer transport bundle

Adds a Node toolchain step that builds platform/emscripten/eduke32-net.js
(the WebRTC+Nostr transport) with esbuild, on its OWN toolchain separate from
emcc, and copies it plus grp-manifest.json into the published site beside
eduke32.js. `.github/workflows/pages.yml` is shared, so this is delivered as a
patch for `main` to apply rather than committed from the transport branch.

Apply from the repo root on the branch that owns pages.yml (wasm/main):

    git apply platform/emscripten/docs/ci-pages.patch

--- a/.github/workflows/pages.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/pages.yml
@@ -39,5 +39,16 @@
       - name: Verify toolchain
         run: emcc --version

+      - name: Set up Node (multiplayer transport bundle)
+        uses: actions/setup-node@v4
+        with:
+          node-version: '22'
+
+      - name: Build multiplayer transport (eduke32-net.js)
+        working-directory: platform/emscripten
+        run: |
+          npm ci
+          npm run build:net
+
       - name: Build (classic software renderer, multi-file)
         run: make PLATFORM=EMSCRIPTEN EM_SINGLE_FILE=0 -j"$(nproc)"
@@ -45,6 +56,8 @@
       - name: Assemble site
         run: |
           mkdir -p _site
           cp eduke32.js eduke32.wasm eduke32.data _site/
           cp platform/emscripten/index.html _site/index.html
+          cp platform/emscripten/eduke32-net.js _site/eduke32-net.js
+          cp platform/emscripten/grp-manifest.json _site/grp-manifest.json
           ls -la _site

NOTE ON LINE NUMBERS: the @@ hunk offsets are approximate for the wasm-branch
pages.yml at the time of writing. If `git apply` reports an offset mismatch, use
`git apply --recount` or apply the two edits by hand — they are:
  1. Insert the two Node steps ("Set up Node…" + "Build multiplayer transport…")
     between the "Verify toolchain" and "Build (classic software renderer…)" steps.
  2. Add the two `cp` lines (eduke32-net.js, grp-manifest.json) to the
     "Assemble site" step, after the index.html copy.

Optionally also run the standalone transport tests as a gate:

      - name: Test multiplayer transport
        working-directory: platform/emscripten
        run: npm test
